---
/**
 * `/guides/deadlines` — from `docs/research/10-compliance-calendar.md`.
 *
 * The instalment dates, the instalment formula, the estimate obligation and
 * the filing-deadline rule are all `verified` there. Penalties and interest
 * (Q26) and whether a separate final-payment date exists beyond the fourth
 * instalment (Q22) are not, and this page says so rather than inventing a
 * rate or a date to fill the gap — per research 10's own framing, "the
 * dates matter more than the arithmetic" for the two priority personas, so
 * this page leads with the dates rather than a computation.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/base-path.ts';
import AsAtStamp from '../../components/AsAtStamp.astro';
import { Callout, CitationRef } from '../../components/ui/index.ts';
import { loadTaxYears } from '../../lib/tax/load.ts';
import '../../styles/guides.css';

const taxYear = loadTaxYears()[0]!.data;
const instalments = [...taxYear.calendar.instalments].sort(
  (a, b) => a.quarter - b.quarter,
);
---

<Base
  title="What are the tax deadlines I need to know for Sri Lanka? — Sri Lanka Tax Return Support"
  description="The four instalment dates through the year, the return filing deadline, and what is not yet confirmed about penalties for missing either."
>
  <div class="guide measure">
    <p class="guide__back"><a href={withBase('/guides/')}>All guides</a></p>

    <h1 class="guide__question">
      What are the tax deadlines I need to know for Sri Lanka?
    </h1>

    <p class="guide__answer">
      Two sets of deadlines, on separate timetables: four{' '}
      <strong>instalment payment</strong> deadlines through the year of assessment, and one{
        ' '
      }
      <strong>return</strong> deadline, due{' '}
      <strong>eight months after the year ends</strong>.{' '}
      <CitationRef
        src="ira-2017#s.93(1)"
        sources={taxYear.sources}
        label="Return deadline from"
      />{' '}
      For Y/A {taxYear.yearOfAssessment} the instalment dates are{' '}
      {
        instalments.map((instalment, index) => (
          <>
            {index > 0 && index === instalments.length - 1
              ? ' and '
              : index > 0
                ? ', '
                : ''}
            <strong>{instalment.due}</strong>
          </>
        ))
      }
      .
    </p>

    <AsAtStamp
      yearOfAssessment={taxYear.yearOfAssessment}
      dataReviewedOn={taxYear.lastReviewed}
    />

    <section class="guide__section">
      <h2>Who has to pay by instalment</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone who derives or expects to derive assessable income during the year from a
        business or an investment, or from an employment where the employer is not
        required to withhold tax, is an instalment payer.{' '}
        <CitationRef src="ira-2017#s.90(1)" sources={taxYear.sources} />{' '}
        That covers freelance and consultancy income paid from outside Sri Lanka, and it covers
        an employee whose pay has no tax deducted from it — see the{' '}
        <a href={withBase('/guides/employer-not-deducting/')}
          >guide on that specific situation</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide__section">
      <h2>The four instalment dates</h2>
      <p>
        On or before the fifteenth day of <strong>August</strong>,{' '}
        <strong>November</strong> and <strong>February</strong> within the year of assessment,
        and the fifteenth of <strong>May</strong> in the{' '}
        <em>following</em> year of assessment.{' '}
        <CitationRef src="ira-2017#s.90(2)(a)" sources={taxYear.sources} />{' '}
        That fourth date is easy to miss because it does not fall inside the year it belongs
        to — a plan built around "four dates within the year" gets it wrong.
      </p>
      <table class="rates-table" data-guide-table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          Instalment due dates for Y/A {taxYear.yearOfAssessment}
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Instalment</th>
            <th scope="col">Due</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            instalments.map((instalment) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Quarter {instalment.quarter}</th>
                <td>{instalment.due}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        These are for Y/A {taxYear.yearOfAssessment}; other years' dates are on the{' '}
        <a href={withBase('/rates/')}>rates page</a> once that year's data is held.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide__section">
      <h2>How much each instalment is</h2>
      <p>
        Not a flat quarter of what you owe. Each instalment is <code>(A − C) / B</code>,
        where A is your own current estimated tax payable, B is the number of instalments
        left including the one being worked out, and C is what you have already paid for
        the year.{' '}
        <CitationRef src="ira-2017#s.90(3)" sources={taxYear.sources} />{' '}
        You are expected to have filed that estimate with the Commissioner-General by the date
        the first instalment falls due.{' '}
        <CitationRef src="ira-2017#s.91(1)" sources={taxYear.sources} />{' '}
        Revising your estimate during the year reshapes every instalment still to come.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide__section">
      <h2>The return itself</h2>
      <p>
        Due <strong>eight months after the end of the year of assessment</strong> — for a year
        running 1 April to 31 March, that is the last day of November.{' '}
        <CitationRef src="ira-2017#s.93(1)" sources={taxYear.sources} />{' '}
        This is a separate deadline from the instalments above, not a summary of them: the instalments
        settle your estimate through the year, and the return is where the actual liability
        is reconciled against what you paid.
      </p>
    </section>

    <Callout
      tone="caution"
      title="What happens if a date is missed is not yet confirmed"
      headingLevel={2}
    >
      <p>
        This project has not confirmed the rate of interest on a late payment or the
        penalty for late filing, so none is stated here — a made-up figure would be worse
        than none. If a date above has already passed for you, that does not mean the
        obligation has gone away; it is worth raising with the Inland Revenue Department
        or a qualified tax practitioner sooner rather than later, since interest most
        likely accrues on each missed instalment individually rather than only from the
        filing deadline.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <section class="guide__section">
      <h2>What this means if this is your situation</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href={withBase('/calculator/')}>calculator</a> shows the instalment schedule
        for your own figures, worked out from the estimate you enter, alongside the computed
        liability itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide__footer">
      <p class="guide__footer-note">
        This is decision support, not tax advice. Verify with the Inland Revenue
        Department or a qualified tax practitioner before you rely on any figure here to
        file or pay.
      </p>
      <ul class="guide__footer-links">
        <li><a href={withBase('/calculator/')}>Work out your figure</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/guides/filing-your-return/')}>Filing your return</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/about/sources/')}>Sources cited on this page</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  [data-guide-table] {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  [data-guide-table] th,
  [data-guide-table] td {
    padding: calc(var(--spacing) * 2) calc(var(--spacing) * 3);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    text-align: start;
  }

  [data-guide-table] thead th {
    border-block-end: 2px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
